en task cannot be completed\\n PROMPT\\n end\\n ```\\n\\n Modify `#call` method (line 22-23):\\n ```ruby\\n def call(prompt)\\n @logger.info(@id, \\\"Starting agent execution\\\")\\n @messages = []\\n @instructions += default_system_prompt # Add this line\\n\\n iteration = 0\\n ```\\n\\n5. Update agents/*.md to focus on WHAT to include in success and failure messages, not HOW to format them.\\n\\n6. Add tests in `spec/ralph/agent_spec.rb`:\\n ```ruby\\n describe '#call' do\\n it 'appends default system prompt to instructions' do\\n agent = Ralph::Agent.new('HAIKU', client: client)\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('SUCCESS:')\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('FAILURE:')\\n end\\n\\n it 'preserves original agent instructions' do\\n agent = Ralph::Agent.new('HAIKU', client: client)\\n expect(agent.instructions).to include('You are a Haiku bot')\\n end\\n end\\n ```\\n\\nPlease review the implementation and verify it meets all requirements in the PRD.\"}","name":"spawnagent"},"id":"call_-7965093745206992737","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"role":"tool","content":"\"## FAILURE\\n\\n### Missing PRD Requirements\\n\\nThe implementation plan requires creating a default system prompt with this specific format:\\n\\n```ruby\\ndef default_system_prompt\\n <<~PROMPT\\n\\n Always return your response in this format:\\n - SUCCESS: {short summary} - when task is complete\\n - FAILURE: {detailed explanation} - when task cannot be completed\\n PROMPT\\nend\\n```\\n\\n**The specs only verify partial content:**\\n- Tests check that `'SUCCESS:'` and `'FAILURE:'` are present in instructions\\n- They do NOT verify the complete format including:\\n - The header \\\"Always return your response in this format:\\\"\\n - The bullet point format \\\"- SUCCESS: {short summary} - when task is complete\\\"\\n - The bullet point format \\\"- FAILURE: {detailed explanation} - when task cannot be completed\\\"\\n\\nThis is a significant gap because the PRD requires specific formatti